### Expected Behaviour

No changes should be reflected other than the Tags update

### Actual Behaviour

Everytime a `terraform plan/apply` is executed, all of the `frontend_ip_configuration` blocks try to rearrange themselves. Nothing changes in the state file even after a successful `terraform apply`. 
There is no actual change being made, whether in the state file or in the actual Azure resource itself.

I've tried two things to try and fix this, with no avail:

1. Tried manually changing the order of the `frontend_ip_configuration` array in the state file to match what the `map(object)` produces
2. Tried to match the order of my Public IP Addresses so they fit the same `frontend_ip_configuration` order, but this doesn't work since Terraform automatically sorts alphabetically by key any `map(object)`.

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Create a Load Balancer in Azure manually (or in our case, via an ARM template, from before our migration to Terraform)
2. Configure the Terraform code
3. Import the state into Terraform
4. Run the Terraform code

